WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.940
Good evening and welcome to the LangFocus Channel.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.880
This is a quick video to bring you some breaking news from the linguistic world.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.180
According to recently released documents.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.900
The E.U. will soon be adopting Esperanto as an official language.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:30.780
For those who don't know, Esperanto Is a constructed language that was created in the 1870s by doctor L. L. Zamenhof.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:37.200
It was created in order to function as an international auxiliary language that people all around the world can learn.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.660
And it was intentionally designed to be extremely easy to learn.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:45.140
But Esperanto never fully caught on and remained mostly a hobby for language nerds.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:45.900
UNTIL NOW.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:52.180
According to E.U officials, Esperanto will be designated the 25th official language of the E.U.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.180
and will function as a working language  of the european parliament,

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.460
as a procedural language of the European Commission,

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.800
in addition to English, French and German

